  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     9240 1451   60
          work is presented in the following papers:              9240 1451   61
          (1) Modern nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS       9240 1451   62
              code system, A.J. Koning and D. Rochman,            9240 1451   63
              A.J. Koning and D. Rochman,                         9240 1451   64
              Nuclear Data Sheets 113 (2012) 2841.                9240 1451   65
          (2) TENDL: Complete Nuclear Data Library for            9240 1451   66
              Innovative Nuclear Science and Technology,          9240 1451   67
              A.J. Koning, D. Rochman, J.Ch Sublet, N. Dzysiuk,   9240 1451   68
              M. Fleming and S. van der Marck,                    9240 1451   69
              Nuclear Data Sheets 155 (2019) 1.                   9240 1451   70
                                                                  9240 1451   71
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           9240 1451   72
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.60, compiled on         9240 1451   73
       Aug  8 2024, 16:13:21 at Villigen   , Switzerland. The RRR 9240 1451   74
       expands from 0 to 6.085682E+1 eV. A total of               9240 1451   75
       3 l-values are used and 431 resonances. The resonance      9240 1451   76
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              9240 1451   77
       The TARES database for the measured resonances is          9240 1451   78
        ->  default up to 0.705435 eV.                            9240 1451   79
       Above this energy, the ladder approach is used.            9240 1451   80
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       9240 1451   81
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          9240 1451   82
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     9240 1451   83
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    9240 1451   84
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  9240 1451   85
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   9240 1451   86
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          9240 1451   87
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       9240 1451   88
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    9240 1451   89
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       9240 1451   90
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         9240 1451   91
       The s-wave average level spacing is 0.705435 eV and        9240 1451   92
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.00017119 1e-4.            9240 1451   93
                                                                  9240 1451   94
  MF33 in the resonance range:                                    9240 1451   95
  The MF33 in the resonance range is obtained by using a number   9240 1451   96
  of MF2 random files. There is therefore a consistency           9240 1451   97
  between the MF2 random and the MF33.                            9240 1451   98
  MF32:                                                           9240 1451   99
