***************************** T A L Y S **************************9240 1451  180
                                                                  9240 1451  181
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   9240 1451  182
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      9240 1451  183
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    9240 1451  184
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     9240 1451  185
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  9240 1451  186
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        9240 1451  187
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    9240 1451  188
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         9240 1451  189
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      9240 1451  190
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    9240 1451  191
stored in this data file:                                         9240 1451  192
                                                                  9240 1451  193
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   9240 1451  194
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     9240 1451  195
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 9240 1451  196
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   9240 1451  197
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                9240 1451  198
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   9240 1451  199
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    9240 1451  200
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        9240 1451  201
- Recoil data                                                     9240 1451  202
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           9240 1451  203
- Total particle energy spectra                                   9240 1451  204
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      9240 1451  205
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        9240 1451  206
- Residual production cross sections                              9240 1451  207
                                                                  9240 1451  208
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            9240 1451  209
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        9240 1451  210
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   9240 1451  211
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                9240 1451  212
                                                                  9240 1451  213
