##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   9240 1451  231
                                                                  9240 1451  232
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 9240 1451  233
                                                                  9240 1451  234
Details about the origin of the resonance parameters for this     9240 1451  235
nuclide are given above in this description. In general, both a   9240 1451  236
Resolved and an Unresolved Resonance Range are given.             9240 1451  237
                                                                  9240 1451  238
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                9240 1451  239
                                                                  9240 1451  240
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       9240 1451  241
calculated with TALYS, possibly normalized to experimental data.  9240 1451  242
If the maximal cross section in an excitation function over the   9240 1451  243
whole energy range does not exceed 1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not  9240 1451  244
included. Cross sections lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have  9240 1451  245
no physical meaning and are set to zero. All MT numbers extend up 9240 1451  246
to the highest incident energy.                                   9240 1451  247
The following reaction channels/MT numbers are generally included:9240 1451  248
                                                                  9240 1451  249
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  9240 1451  250
                                                                  9240 1451  251
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range,    9240 1451  252
or partly reproduced using experimental data.                     9240 1451  253
                                                                  9240 1451  254
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     9240 1451  255
                                                                  9240 1451  256
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    9240 1451  257
total cross section.                                              9240 1451  258
                                                                  9240 1451  259
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            9240 1451  260
                                                                  9240 1451  261
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    9240 1451  262
                                                                  9240 1451  263
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        9240 1451  264
                                                                  9240 1451  265
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  9240 1451  266
                                                                  9240 1451  267
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           9240 1451  268
                                                                  9240 1451  269
MT5 contains the reactions which can not be stored in any other   9240 1451  270
MT-number. The information of MF3/MT5 can be combined with        9240 1451  271
MF6/MT5 to obtain residual production cross sections particle     9240 1451  272
production cross sections and (double-)differential cross         9240 1451  273
sections.                                                         9240 1451  274
                                                                  9240 1451  275
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 9240 1451  276
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 9240 1451  277
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 9240 1451  278
- MT28     : (n,np) cross section                                 9240 1451  279
- MT51-90  : (n,n') cross section for 1st-40th excited state      9240 1451  280
- MT91     : (n,n') continuum cross section                       9240 1451  281
- MT102    : (n,gamma) cross section                              9240 1451  282
- MT103    : (n,p) cross section                                  9240 1451  283
- MT104    : (n,d) cross section                                  9240 1451  284
- MT105    : (n,t) cross section                                  9240 1451  285
- MT106    : (n,h) cross section                                  9240 1451  286
- MT107    : (n,a) cross section                                  9240 1451  287
- MT600-610: (n,p) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       9240 1451  288
- MT649    : (n,p) continuum cross section                        9240 1451  289
- MT650-655: (n,d) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        9240 1451  290
- MT699    : (n,d) continuum cross section                        9240 1451  291
- MT700-705: (n,t) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        9240 1451  292
- MT749    : (n,t) continuum cross section                        9240 1451  293
- MT750-755: (n,h) cross section for 0th-5th excited state        9240 1451  294
- MT799    : (n,h) continuum cross section                        9240 1451  295
- MT800-810: (n,a) cross section for 0th-10th excited state       9240 1451  296
- MT849    : (n,a) continuum cross section                        9240 1451  297
                                                                  9240 1451  298
##### MF4: ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY PARTICLES           9240 1451  299
                                                                  9240 1451  300
We use MF4 for the neutron scattering angular distribution for    9240 1451  301
discrete levels.                                                  9240 1451  302
                                                                  9240 1451  303
- MT2      : Elastic angular distribution                         9240 1451  304
                                                                  9240 1451  305
The flag LTT=3 is used to indicate a switch at some high energy,  9240 1451  306
generally 50 MeV, from a Legendre representation to a tabulated   9240 1451  307
representation. For incident energies below this energy, the      9240 1451  308
Legendre coefficients are given on a sufficiently precise energy  9240 1451  309
grid. They are a sum of calculated Legendre coefficients for      9240 1451  310
compound nucleus and shape-elastic scattering. For higher         9240 1451  311
incident energies, relative angular distributions are tabulated   9240 1451  312
on an angular grid.                                               9240 1451  313
                                                                  9240 1451  314
- MT51-70  : (n,n') angular distribution for 1st-20th state       9240 1451  315
- MT600-610: (n,p) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        9240 1451  316
- MT650-655: (n,d) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         9240 1451  317
- MT700-705: (n,t) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         9240 1451  318
- MT750-755: (n,h) angular distribution for 0th-5th state         9240 1451  319
- MT800-810: (n,a) angular distribution for 0th-10th state        9240 1451  320
                                                                  9240 1451  321
##### MF5: FISSION NEUTRON SPECTRUM                               9240 1451  322
                                                                  9240 1451  323
The data for the fission neutron spectrum are provided by the     9240 1451  324
TANES code[kon19]. Both prompt and delayed spectra are given.     9240 1451  325
                                                                  9240 1451  326
- MT18     : Prompt fission neutron spectrum                      9240 1451  327
                                                                  9240 1451  328
- MT455    : Delayed fission neutron spectrum                     9240 1451  329
                                                                  9240 1451  330
##### MF6: PRODUCT ENERGY-ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS                     9240 1451  331
                                                                  9240 1451  332
In MF6 we store all secondary energy, angle, and energy-angle     9240 1451  333
distributions, as well as all residual and discrete + continuum   9240 1451  334
photon production cross sections for channels other than capture  9240 1451  335
(MT102) and reactions to discrete levels (MT51,etc.).             9240 1451  336
All data are generated with TALYS.                                9240 1451  337
                                                                  9240 1451  338
- MT5      : (n,anything) yields and energy-angle distributions   9240 1451  339
                                                                  9240 1451  340
MT5 contains, in this order,                                      9240 1451  341
For neutrons up to alpha particles and photons:                   9240 1451  342
- the production yields per particle for the whole energy range   9240 1451  343
- the secondary energy-angle distributions per particles which are9240 1451  344
  not represented by explicit MT numbers. On a secondary energy   9240 1451  345
  grid the relative emission spectra are given together with the  9240 1451  346
  parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular              9240 1451  347
  distributions. Inelastic scattering cross sections for discrete 9240 1451  348
  states have been broadened and added to the continuum spectra.  9240 1451  349
For each residual product:                                        9240 1451  350
- the production yields for the whole energy range.               9240 1451  351
- the recoil                                                      9240 1451  352
These distributions can be multiplied with MF3/MT5 to get         9240 1451  353
the production cross sections and (double-)differential cross     9240 1451  354
sections.                                                         9240 1451  355
                                                                  9240 1451  356
- MT16     : (n,2n) energy-angle distr. and photon production     9240 1451  357
                                                                  9240 1451  358
First, for each type of outgoing particle, the (trivial) integer  9240 1451  359
particle yields are given. Next, on a sufficiently dense incident 9240 1451  360
energy grid the secondary energy-angle distributions are          9240 1451  361
specified by means of the relative emission spectra and the       9240 1451  362
parameters for the Kalbach systematics for angular distributions. 9240 1451  363
Next, the photon yield is tabulated as a function of incident     9240 1451  364
energy. For each incident energy, the photon production is given  9240 1451  365
for all discrete gamma lines present in the final nucleus. A      9240 1451  366
continuum photon distribution is added to this. We assume         9240 1451  367
isotropy for all produced gamma rays.                             9240 1451  368
                                                                  9240 1451  369
For the following MT-numbers, the same procedure as for MT16 is   9240 1451  370
followed:                                                         9240 1451  371
                                                                  9240 1451  372
- MT17 : (n,3n) energy-angle distr. and photon production         9240 1451  373
- MT22 : (n,na) energy-angle distr. and photon production         9240 1451  374
- MT28 : (n,np) energy-angle distr. and photon production         9240 1451  375
- MT91 : (n,n') continuum energy-angle distr. and phot. prod.     9240 1451  376
- MT649: (n,p) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9240 1451  377
- MT699: (n,d) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9240 1451  378
- MT749: (n,t) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9240 1451  379
- MT809: (n,h) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9240 1451  380
- MT849: (n,a) continuum energy-angle distr. and photon prod.     9240 1451  381
                                                                  9240 1451  382
##### MF8: RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                 9240 1451  383
                                                                  9240 1451  384
For reactions to isomers, MF8 designates where the information    9240 1451  385
for isomeric versus ground state production, or residual          9240 1451  386
production can be found, i.e. for each MT number it points to     9240 1451  387
either MF6, MF9 or MF10.                                          9240 1451  388
                                                                  9240 1451  389
##### MF9: MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES  9240 1451  390
                                                                  9240 1451  391
MF9 is used for isomer production by non-threshold reactions.     9240 1451  392
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    9240 1451  393
as isomer.                                                        9240 1451  394
                                                                  9240 1451  395
##### MF10: CROSS SECTIONS FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES 9240 1451  396
                                                                  9240 1451  397
MF10 is used for isomer production by threshold reactions.        9240 1451  398
Final states with a lifetime that exceeds 1 second are treated    9240 1451  399
as isomer.                                                        9240 1451  400
                                                                  9240 1451  401
##### MF12: PHOTON PRODUCTION YIELD DATA                          9240 1451  402
                                                                  9240 1451  403
MF12 is used for the photon production for two types of reactions:9240 1451  404
- Reactions to discrete levels (MT51, etc.) For this transition   9240 1451  405
  probabilities are used (LO=2)                                   9240 1451  406
- Photons from neutron capture (MT102). Here multiplicities are   9240 1451  407
  given                                                           9240 1451  408
                                                                  9240 1451  409
##### MF14: PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                          9240 1451  410
                                                                  9240 1451  411
All photon production is considered as isotropic                  9240 1451  412
                                                                  9240 1451  413
##### MF15: PHOTON ENERGY SPECTRA                                 9240 1451  414
                                                                  9240 1451  415
For capture (MT102), the photon energy spectrum is given.         9240 1451  416
                                                                  9240 1451  417
##### MF31: COVARIANCES OF AVERAGE FISSION NEUTRON DATA           9240 1451  418
                                                                  9240 1451  419
The covariance data for the number of fission neutrons are        9240 1451  420
provided by the TAFIS code[kon19]. On the basis of rather simple  9240 1451  421
assumptions a full covariance file for the total nubar is         9240 1451  422
obtained.                                                         9240 1451  423
                                                                  9240 1451  424
##### MF32: COVARIANCES OF RESONANCE PARAMETERS                   9240 1451  425
                                                                  9240 1451  426
In MF32, we store the covariances of resonance parameters,        9240 1451  427
and more details are given above in this description. In most     9240 1451  428
versions of TENDL, this information is now stored in MF33.        9240 1451  429
                                                                  9240 1451  430
##### MF33: COVARIANCES OF NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS                 9240 1451  431
                                                                  9240 1451  432
In MF33, we store the covariances of most, but not all, reaction  9240 1451  433
channels that are given in MF3. All covariances are generated     9240 1451  434
with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates TALYS runs using    9240 1451  435
a Monte Carlo parameter method.                                   9240 1451  436
For each MT-number, the information consists of:                  9240 1451  437
1. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Ea (variances)                9240 1451  438
2. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTa, Eb (correlations for the      9240 1451  439
   same reaction channel between different energies)              9240 1451  440
3. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Ea (correlations between      9240 1451  441
   different reaction channels for the same energy)               9240 1451  442
4. Covariances for MTa, Ea and MTb, Eb (correlations between      9240 1451  443
   different reaction channels for different energies)            9240 1451  444
Classes 1 and 2 are covered by NI-type subsubsections with        9240 1451  445
flag LB=5, followed by a LB=8 section which contains              9240 1451  446
the cross section variances multiplied by 1.e-3. Next, classes 3  9240 1451  447
and 4 are covered by flag LB=6 to account for the different       9240 1451  448
energy grids that two correlating MT-sections may have. Since     9240 1451  449
the total correlation matrix is fully symmetric, we only need to  9240 1451  450
include the correlation elements between different MT-numbers     9240 1451  451
once, and we do that in the subsection with the lowest of the     9240 1451  452
two MT-numbers. We include covariance information for all the     9240 1451  453
total cross sections, the lumped partial cross sections and the   9240 1451  454
individual inelastic cross sections per level (MT51,...). We do   9240 1451  455
not include covariances for MT600 and higher MT-numbers. For the  9240 1451  456
most important channels, we include cross-channel correlations.   9240 1451  457
                                                                  9240 1451  458
##### MF34: COVARIANCES OF ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS                  9240 1451  459
                                                                  9240 1451  460
In MF34, we store the covariances of the elastic scattering       9240 1451  461
angular distributions that are given in MF4/MT2. All covariances  9240 1451  462
are generated with the TASMAN code [kon19], which generates       9240 1451  463
TALYS runs using a Monte Carlo parameter method. The tables are   9240 1451  464
restricted to MT2 and contain covariances for the first 6         9240 1451  465
Legendre coefficients. Both intra- and inter-correlations of the  9240 1451  466
various Legendre coefficients are given. As in MF33, the LB5      9240 1451  467
representation is used.                                           9240 1451  468
                                                                  9240 1451  469
##### MF35: COVARIANCES OF FISSION NEUTRON SPECTRUM               9240 1451  470
                                                                  9240 1451  471
The covariance data for fission neutron spectra are provided by   9240 1451  472
the TANES code[kon19]. The contents of MF35 are covariance data   9240 1451  473
between different outgoing energies of the neutron spectra.       9240 1451  474
                                                                  9240 1451  475
##### MF40: COVARIANCES OF ISOMER PRODUCTION                      9240 1451  476
                                                                  9240 1451  477
For covariances of ground state and isomeric cross sections, the  9240 1451  478
same procedures as for MF33 are used.                             9240 1451  479
                                                                  9240 1451  480
